!===============================================================================
            Electron collision reactions
!-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cross sections used are from:
- Itikawa database, www.lxcat.net, retrieved on March 31, 2014.
- Hayashi database, www.lxcat.net, retrieved on March 31, 2014.
- R. K. Janev and D. Reiter, Phys Plasmas 11 (2004) 780-829.

To model the discharge process, these electron collision reactions were considered.
Reaction rates can be computed using BOLSIG+ as a function of E/N.
Collisions of O2 with electrons contributing 4.5 eV are considered dissociative

O2       + E       = O        + O        + E                                 
O2       + E       = O        + O(D)     + E                                 
O2       + E       = O2(A)    + E                                            
O2       + E       = O2(B)    + E                                                                                                                   
O2       + E       = O2+      + E        + E                                 
O2       + E       = O        + O+       + E      + E                      
O2       + E       = O        + O-                                                                     
C2H4     + E       = C2H3     + H        + E                                 
C2H4     + E       = C2H2     + H2       + E                                 
C2H4     + E       = C2H2     + H        + H      + E                      
C2H4     + E       = C2H      + H2       + H      + E    
C2H4 	 + E 	   = C2H4(+)  + E	     + E 
C2H4 	 + E 	   = C2H3(+)  + H		 + E	  + E 
C2H4 	 + E 	   = C2H2(+)  + H 		 + H	  + E	+ E
C2H4 	 + E 	   = C2H2(+)  + H2		 + E	  + E                                     
Ar       + E       = Ar*      + E                                                                                      
Ar       + E       = Ar(+)    + E        + E                                 
                             